{"authored" [{"question" "q-24488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})-{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948787/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a8484b8e96bb9ad1d23dd13ec360247c96845d6fa5803f133795e3d9042389f" "basis" 556 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948787/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-24488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948787/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "38385a60601907b35689e519c2e0453a8d1508821e6860a3956ce5f6cd72e086" "basis" 556 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948787/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-24488" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948787/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a8484b8e96bb9ad1d23dd13ec360247c96845d6fa5803f133795e3d9042389f" "basis" 556 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948787/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\sqrt{3}{cos}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}-\\sqrt{3}{sin}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/referen