ake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953503/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953503/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2c1ee6f201c5269972a6dc4688de299dc2c3d7d6dcd545be77f061a2966df5c" "basis" 614 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953503/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953503/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2c1ee6f201c5269972a6dc4688de299dc2c3d7d6dcd545be77f061a2966df5c" "basis" 614 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953503/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-120353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $5{cos}^{2}⁡{16}^{∘}-5{sin}^{2}⁡{16}^{∘}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039198/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff865529cd1e353975032747b454336e536dcf6ab158595a80f7f271778caed6"} {"question" "q-120353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n5({cos}^{2}⁡{16}^{∘}-{sin}^{2}⁡{16}^{∘})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={16}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡{16}^{∘}-{sin}^{2}⁡{16}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {16}^{∘})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5({cos}^{2}⁡{16}^{∘}-{sin}^{2}⁡{16}^{∘}) & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039198/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff865529cd1e353975032747b454336e536dcf6ab158595a80f7f271778caed6"} {"question" "q-120353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039198/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6a6df37f14697ffad44d694f927c71ac8192e51adc7d53d7df050442bf270d71"} {"question" "q-120353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039198/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff865529cd1e353975032747b454336e536dcf6ab158595a80f7f271778caed6"} {"question" "q-120353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\operatorname{cos}⁡{16}^{∘}"] ["math" "10\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}"] ["math" "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡{16}^{∘}"] ["math" "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039198/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff865529cd1e353975032747b454336e536dcf6ab158595a80f7f271778caed6"} {"question" "q-120353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039198/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff865529cd1e353975032747b454336e536dcf6ab158595a80f7f271778caed6"} {"question" "q-76401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $3{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-3{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})$ as a single trigonometric ratio." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039198/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff865529cd1e353975032747b454336e536dcf6ab158595a80f7f271778caed6"} {"question" "q-76401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n3({cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}))\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039198/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff865529cd1e353975032747b454336e536dcf6ab158595a80f7f271778caed6"} {"question" "q-76401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039198/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6a6df37f14697ffad44d694f927c71ac8192e51adc7d53d7df050442bf270d71"} {"question" "q-76401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039198/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff865529cd1e353975032747b454336e536dcf6ab158595a80f7f271778caed6"} {"question" "q